---
/* Component — CardTitleBadge
 * A small label above the card title — a short qualifier such as a status or a
 * category. Plain text, deliberately not a pill: daisyUI's own .badge carries a
 * border, background and --radius-selector, none of which are wanted here, so
 * it is not rented.
 *
 * Renders as a sibling *before* CardTitle, never nested inside it. daisyUI's
 * .card-title is a flex row (align-items:center; gap:.5rem), so a nested badge
 * would sit beside the title rather than above it.
 *
 * Typography is transcribed from text.css's .text-label, built from the same
 * semantic tokens; see Card for why the declarations live here rather than
 * referencing that class.
 *
 * Three taste decisions were left at their most faithful value rather than
 * invented, and want a look at the rendered preview:
 *   - <p> as the element. <small> would add "side comment" semantics that may
 *     not be wanted; a <span> would need forcing to block.
 *   - No colour. .text-label sets none, so the badge inherits the card's text
 *     colour; muted may read better for a qualifier.
 *   - No margin. .text-label sets none and Tailwind's preflight zeroes the
 *     browser default, so the badge sits flush above the title. */
---

<p>
  <slot />
</p>

<style>
  p {
    font-family: var(--bravoixr-font-body);
    font-size: var(--bravoixr-text-label);
    font-weight: var(--bravoixr-weight-label);
    line-height: var(--bravoixr-leading-prose);
    letter-spacing: var(--bravoixr-tracking-prose);
  }
</style>
